1. **A method of fabricating a magnetoresistive random-access memory (MRAM) device, the method comprising:**  

   forming a magnetic tunnel junction (MTJ) stack over a substrate, the MTJ stack comprising a reference magnetic layer, a tunnel-barrier layer, and a free magnetic layer;  

   patterning the MTJ stack to form a preliminary MTJ pillar having a first lateral width, wherein the patterning produces redeposited metallic material on a sidewall of the preliminary MTJ pillar;  

   forming a sacrificial dielectric layer over the preliminary MTJ pillar, including along the sidewall and over the redeposited metallic material;  

   performing a sidewall-cleaning process that removes the sacrificial dielectric layer from the sidewall and removes at least a portion of the redeposited metallic material; and  

   laterally recessing at least one layer of the preliminary MTJ pillar during or after the sidewall-cleaning process to form a cleaned MTJ pillar having a second lateral width smaller than the first lateral width.

**1. A method of forming a magnetic tunnel junction device, the method comprising:**  
forming a magnetic tunnel junction stack on an electrode, the magnetic tunnel junction stack comprising a magnetic reference layer, a tunnel barrier layer, and a magnetic free layer;  
patterning the magnetic tunnel junction stack to define a magnetic tunnel junction pillar having a first lateral dimension and a sidewall, wherein the patterning produces metal redeposition on the sidewall;  
removing the metal redeposition from the sidewall; and  
after removing the metal redeposition, laterally etching the magnetic tunnel junction pillar to reduce the first lateral dimension to a second lateral dimension.
